but me, cloak and tunic as clothes, that woman
very fine, having clothed me in, and sandals for my feet having given,
sent forth to the field;

And from the lady, then, not anything soothing is it possible to hear,
neither word nor any deed, since an evil has fallen upon the house,
men overweening;

And we two, in the hut, drinking and feasting,
in each other's sorrows let us take pleasure, pitiful ones,
recalling them;

but me they snatched away, Taphian raiders, men,
from the field as I came, and sold me, having brought me here,
to this man's house;

